#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# acosh

#% text
# `acosh(z)` gives the inverse hyperbolic cosine.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For complex `z` the principal value is `log(z + sqrt(z + 1)*sqrt(z - 1))`.

#% item
# Exact special values and odd symmetry are applied; other exact arguments stay unevaluated.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
acosh(-1)
#% output
#= 1im*pi

#% cell
acosh(2.0)
#% output
#= 1.3169578969248166

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
acosh(0.5)
#% output
#= complex(-1.1102230246251565e-16, 1.0471975511965976)

#% text
# 30 digits:

#% cell
n(acosh(1/3), 30)
#% output
#= complex(ball(9.5380346309689672326e-36, 2.54e-35), 1.23095941734077468213492917824799)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `log`, `atan`, `asin`, `acos`
